  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "BREAKING: 'nem run' now requires the '--' separator before a tool's arguments ('nem run ng -- serve'). Every proxy already passes it, so typing 'ng serve' is unaffected; only direct 'nem run' calls that left it out change. An argument that would not reach the tool is refused now instead of being dropped in silence.\nNew 'nem which <tool>' explains which copy of a tool a typed name runs - the system one, the env's, or a project's - and why, step by step. 'nem run' starts what the same resolver returns, so the explanation cannot drift from the behaviour. 'nem tool list' gained a Command column with the same verdict, and reports a project copy as 'via nem (local copy <version>)' rather than claiming it always takes over.\nThe project config is now JSONC: 'nem init' creates nem.jsonc with an explanatory header, and comments are allowed in it. The config also carries a schema version now, so a config written by a newer nem is refused with a clear message instead of being half-read. Existing nem.json envs keep working unchanged - nem reads either name and writes back to the one the project already has.\nMistyped commands and other input errors print a plain message with a suggestion instead of a stack trace.",
